---
import QuickKata from '../../components/QuickKata.astro';
import SeedReportCheck from '../../components/SeedReportCheck.astro';
import { seedSalesCsv } from '../../data/seed-sales';

const prompt = `You are my data-quality partner. Clean this fictional seed-sale dataset and write a short, honest report.

Rules:
- Treat exact duplicate rows as one sale. Treat item names without regard to capitalization.
- Do not guess missing quantities or non-numeric prices. Put incomplete rows in an exceptions list.
- Calculate quantities and revenue only for complete, unique rows. Show your arithmetic.
- Report the number of rows received, exact duplicates removed, complete unique sales and exceptions.
- Include a short table of the clean rows and a short plain-language summary.
- This is synthetic practice data: do not describe the sales as real or invent missing values.

Here is the CSV:\n\n${seedSalesCsv}`;
---
<QuickKata
  title="Rescue messy data"
  description="Turn a small, messy spreadsheet into a useful report you can check."
  time="About 10 minutes"
  prompt={prompt}
  exampleHref="/examples/seed-sales-messy.csv"
  exampleLabel="Download the practice CSV"
  exampleNote="This is fictional practice data created for the kata. The figures below are calculated from the dataset, not real sales."
>
  <article slot="outcome" class="report">
    <p class="tag">Example result · synthetic data</p>
    <h3>A report you can trust</h3>
    <div class="numbers"><p><strong>4</strong> complete sales</p><p><strong>2</strong> need review</p><p><strong>$22</strong> complete sales total</p></div>
    <p>Seven rows came in. Remove one exact duplicate, then set aside the two rows with missing or invalid values. The four complete sales contain seven items: six Basil for $18 and one Mint for $4. Try the checks by hand or use the assistant prompt below.</p>
  </article>
  <div slot="verify">
    <ol>
      <li>Check that the repeated S102 row is counted once, and that S104 and S105 are listed as exceptions.</li>
      <li>Check the complete rows: 2 × $3, 1 × $4, 3 × $3 and 1 × $3. The total is $22 across seven items.</li>
      <li>Check that “Basil” and “basil” are grouped together and that missing values were not invented.</li>
      <li>If a check fails, tell your assistant exactly which row is wrong and ask for a corrected report.</li>
    </ol>
    <SeedReportCheck />
    <p><strong>Remix:</strong> use a small dataset you are allowed to share, and define how to handle duplicates and missing values before calculating.</p>
  </div>
</QuickKata>
<style>
  .report { padding: var(--space-5); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--paper-raised); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .report h3 { margin-top: 0; }
  .tag { color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: 700; }
  .numbers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 8rem), 1fr)); gap: var(--space-3); }
  .numbers p { padding: var(--space-3); background: var(--paper-sunk); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  .numbers strong { display: block; font-size: var(--text-2xl); }
</style>
